In addition to the above methods, nioBuffer and nioBuffers methods should return read-only ByteBuffer instances. While looking into this I noticed that the override for nioBuffer exists in ReadOnlyByteBufferBuf, but the nioBuffers override is missing.

Something like this for making nioBuffer and nioBuffers return read-only ByteBuffers?
```java
    @Override
    public ByteBuffer nioBuffer(int index, int length) {
        return unwrap().nioBuffer(index, length).asReadOnlyBuffer();
    }

    @Override
    public ByteBuffer[] nioBuffers(int index, int length) {
        ByteBuffer[] byteBuffers = unwrap().nioBuffers(index, length);
        for (int i = 0; i < byteBuffers.length; i++) {
            byteBuffers[i] = byteBuffers[i].asReadOnlyBuffer();
        }
        return byteBuffers;
    }
```

